# Chance-Met Elves: "Whenever you scry" is its controller's scry, and a scry only. Bot1 casts the Elves on turn 1. On turn
# 2 Bot2 casts Preordain and scries 2: Bot1's Elves do not trigger (no counter). On turn 3 Bot1 casts Consider, which
# surveils (CR 701.25), not scries: still no counter. Then Bot1 casts Preordain and scries 2: the Elves trigger, one
# counter, so the turn's "only once" was not spent by the surveil.

